{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans","id":522367,"title":"DO Vampires/Kuei-jin/Fera believe they are more superior to Humans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-20T13:22:24-07:00","id":522367,"title":"DO Vampires/Kuei-jin/Fera believe they are more superior to Humans?","content":"Like do they think they are the master race?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T13:57:22-07:00","id":522485,"title":"","content":"Vampires? Plenty of them, especially elders and followers of the Paths of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Kuei-Jin? Depends on the Dharma and the individual. The core Five Dharmas and some of the sides ones basically hold that humans have their place in the order of things just as they do and should be respected as such. Of course that doesn't stop them from manipulating things. Then there's a Dharma that states the Kuei-Jin are demi-gods on the path to becoming gods.<br /> <br /> Fera? Short of. Technically they aren't supposed to but... well there's plenty of Kinfolk that would call that BS. And it did kind of create the most infamous of CWoD denizens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T14:04:43-07:00","id":522491,"title":"","content":"There are waaaaaay too fucking many Vampires/Kuei-Jin/Fera to make a blanket statement on their personal beliefs like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T14:29:20-07:00","id":522551,"title":"","content":"Do you believe you are a member of the master race?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T14:34:05-07:00","id":522556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=522551#post522551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you believe you are a member of the master race?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I was a supernatural..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T14:49:39-07:00","id":522566,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's too much of a stretch to say that many supernatural beings in the WoD believe they are of a superior order to humanity. Many Sabbat certainly do, explicitly so. Elders of any sect save those with human belief systems probably do. I would imagine many animal-born shapeshifters do.<br /> <br /> And then when a Sword of Heimdall and a ghoul of Totentanz love each other and white people so much they just can't help themselves... :P<br /> <br /> Not to mention the recent uptick in blatantly racist Kha'vadi in M20. They literally call the modern world a &quot;white-mare.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T15:09:56-07:00","id":522581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morimaruvik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=522566#post522566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then when a Sword of Heimdall and a ghoul of Totentanz love each other and white people so much they just can't help themselves... :P</div> </div> </div> </div>...The main body of the Fenrir kill them and make fun of Totenfurter for such apalling use of German? (^VVVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T15:10:42-07:00","id":522582,"title":"","content":"In general, yes, supernatural beings in the CWoD look down on humans. In many cases, they see humans as nothing more than chattel to be exploited or vermin to be exterminated. Obviously, there are exceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T16:06:14-07:00","id":522620,"title":"","content":"In general, yes, the super powerful, sometimes immortal creatures of the world of darkness believe themselves superior to mortals (mostly because they are). (The exception probably being wraiths).<br /> <br /> The mortals that stand out usually either die horribly or, in the case of vampires, get turned into vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5540-drakilian","name":"Drakilian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T21:11:54-07:00","id":522904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans#post522367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like do they think they are the master race?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No of course not, that's like a person thinking they are a master Cow or master rat. Normal humans are so much lower on the scale of contempt by supernaturals broadly speaking on a cultural level than mere racism, individuals of course may have different visions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T00:55:00-07:00","id":524151,"title":"","content":"I've played a Shadow Lord Theurge that was envious of human ability to 'take the blue pill' and live a normal life.<br /> I've also played a Simba Urban Maneater in a rougher game.<br /> <br /> But for the most part, they tend to be more in the middle. Power Constrained vs No Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T14:43:07-07:00","id":524758,"title":"","content":"The standard Kuei-jin line is a definte no. Kuei-jin are sinners, that's the mythological reason that they are what they are. They're people who escaped Hell by the sheer force of their darker side. Further, while mortals are capable of gaining enlightenment or at least being reincarnated as part of the natural cycle of the world, the Kuei-jin have broken off from that cycle. You could see that as a good thing (and presumably akuma do just that), but theologically that's not how most see it.<br /> <br /> That said, in practice they act in a superior manner towards the masses of humanity. That's their role, or so they believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T17:44:18-07:00","id":524948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=524758#post524758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The standard Kuei-jin line is a definte no. Kuei-jin are sinners, that's the mythological reason that they are what they are. They're people who escaped Hell by the sheer force of their darker side. Further, while mortals are capable of gaining enlightenment or at least being reincarnated as part of the natural cycle of the world, the Kuei-jin have broken off from that cycle. You could see that as a good thing (and presumably akuma do just that), but theologically that's not how most see it.<br /> <br /> That said, in practice they act in a superior manner towards the masses of humanity. That's their role, or so they believe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They are also something that can freely be killed and a source of food(look at the whole sidebar on child slavery). KJ as individuals are driven to treat humans better as a culture though they are corrupt as any other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T13:36:12-07:00","id":525856,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that while the Kindred of the West may, in many cases see view themselves as a higher order than mortal human beings (the Sabbat especially, although the Camarilla and Independents are by no means exempt from this), they fear humanity more than any other threat.<br /> <br /> Event the Sabbat fears mortals. They spit and rant about their superiority to human beings, make a show of disdaining even the practice of keeping ghouls, but then they quietly adhere to their own version of the Masquerade. Sure, they want to go back to the dark ages, where vampires ruled openly over the Kine, but they're not really rushing to make that happen, in great part because they realize it's a pipe-dream - the burning times changed everything, and even if the Sabbat doesn't want to admit it, they can't deny it.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Cainites tend to look down on humans as inferior, and then they lock themselves away in dark basements, huddled behind reenforced doors, guarded by armed ghouls whenever the sun rises.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T23:57:13-07:00","id":526438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=525856#post525856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that while the Kindred of the West may, in many cases see view themselves as a higher order than mortal human beings (the Sabbat especially, although the Camarilla and Independents are by no means exempt from this), they fear humanity more than any other threat.<br /> <br /> Event the Sabbat fears mortals. They spit and rant about their superiority to human beings, make a show of disdaining even the practice of keeping ghouls, but then they quietly adhere to their own version of the Masquerade. Sure, they want to go back to the dark ages, where vampires ruled openly over the Kine, but they're not really rushing to make that happen, in great part because they realize it's a pipe-dream - the burning times changed everything, and even if the Sabbat doesn't want to admit it, they can't deny it.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Cainites tend to look down on humans as inferior, and then they lock themselves away in dark basements, huddled behind reenforced doors, guarded by armed ghouls whenever the sun rises.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Compare that to the action of humans in any zombie movie. Fear of the mass doesn't mean they don't think they are superior individually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T12:25:52-07:00","id":526936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=525856#post525856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that while the Kindred of the West may, in many cases see view themselves as a higher order than mortal human beings (the Sabbat especially, although the Camarilla and Independents are by no means exempt from this), they fear humanity more than any other threat.<br /> <br /> Event the Sabbat fears mortals. They spit and rant about their superiority to human beings, make a show of disdaining even the practice of keeping ghouls, but then they quietly adhere to their own version of the Masquerade. Sure, they want to go back to the dark ages, where vampires ruled openly over the Kine, but they're not really rushing to make that happen, in great part because they realize it's a pipe-dream - the burning times changed everything, and even if the Sabbat doesn't want to admit it, they can't deny it.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Cainites tend to look down on humans as inferior, and then they lock themselves away in dark basements, huddled behind reenforced doors, guarded by armed ghouls whenever the sun rises.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well that's just not true at all. A single neonate vampire could easily destroy all of humanity by simple virtue of the fact that it can replicate near constantly with huge ease and enslave others ridiculously easily through use of his blood. A single vampire can create an infinite number of other vampires, as well as a near infinite number of slaves - each of which is stronger and much harder to kill than any normal human.<br /> <br /> The <i>reason</i> vampires don't do that is because it would be stupid. Destroying your very best food source is counterproductive to your chances of survival.<br /> <br /> Vampires could enslave all of humanity as well, but then they'd have to destroy too many humans in order to keep the numbers of slaves manageable. Frankly, it's just easier to work more subtly.<br /> <br /> Mages? A sufficiently powerful mage could annihalate the world with a single spell. They're just insanely powerful - and Paradox takes far too long to build up to actually dangerous levels.<br /> <br /> Werewolves? I'm not sure most humans are even actually capable of harming werewolves.<br /> <br /> Comparing the supernaturals* to the mortals will always end with the mortals losing, the reason humanity isn't enslaved is either because it would be counterproductive (vampires), not worth it (werewolves) or not conductive to their goals (mages).<br /> <br /> What I imagine generally keeps humanity from being gang-banged by an orgy of supernatural forces is that if any supernatural race ever actually did do something like this, they would be immediately targeted by all the other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> *Changelings are weak enough that humanity is a serious threat to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5540-drakilian","user":"Drakilian","date":". 05-24-2015, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5540-drakilian","name":"Drakilian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T21:48:43-07:00","id":527346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=526438#post526438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare that to the action of humans in any zombie movie. Fear of the mass doesn't mean they don't think they are superior individually.</div> </div> </div> </div>This analogy breaks down too quickly though. Yes, the idea is that Vampires can't face humanity en mass, but they didn't seem to care much about that in the Dark Ages. It isn't just humanity's numbers, it's their technology and organization. It's precisely the intelligence of humans, their resourcefulness and their ability to work together that makes them dangerous. The Masquerade came about in the Renaissance - this is after the Black Death killed off a third or more of the population a hundred years prior.<br /> <br /> Comparatively, Zombies are mindless. They even lack the predatory cunning of a Wight Vampire. They don't work together, they just throw themselves at their prey en mass. The horror you feel from being hunted by a Zombie is their relentlessness, the inevitability of their victory.<br /> <br /> With a vampire fearing the throng of humanity, it's much different. It's the fear of an apex predator suddenly realizing they aren't top of the food chain anymore. It's the fear of being systematically hunted down, having your weaknesses discovered and exploited.<br /> <br /> You're absolutely right, they're going to consider an individual human being to be their inferior. But they wouldn't have created a world-wide system of government dedicated to hiding their existence from humans if they were so convinced of their superiority (this is the point the Sabbat made when it formed - that hiding was an admission that vampires were weak enough to fear humans. Naturally, 500 years down the line, the Sabbat's quietly fallen in line with the policy of secrecy).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakilian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=526936#post526936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's just not true at all. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Why do you think the Masquerade came about?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakilian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=526936#post526936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A single neonate vampire could easily destroy all of humanity by simple virtue of the fact that it can replicate near constantly with huge ease and enslave others ridiculously easily through use of his blood. A single vampire can create an infinite number of other vampires, as well as a near infinite number of slaves - each of which is stronger and much harder to kill than any normal human.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean &quot;theoretically destroy all of humanity,&quot; not &quot;easily destroy all of humanity.&quot;<br /> <br /> A single neonate vampire can be neutralized by a pool-cue snapped in two. He can easily overpower 2 or 3 people, sure, but he can't fight off 20 people at the same time, all by himself. He can't fight off an entire SWAT team laying into him with modern weaponry, even if he is only taking Bashing damage. And he certainly can't do anything if they stake him while he's sleeping the day away and drag him out into the sun.<br /> <br /> Mortal vampire hunters are responsible for driving vampires underground, because the Elders were scared enough that they tossed their neonates at the humans, who promptly lit them up in big old bonfires. That directly led to the formation of the Sabbat, when the younger vampires got rightfully pissed off that their Elders were throwing them under the bus... or onto the pyre, as the case may be.<br /> <br /> Even an Elder's helpless when the sun comes up.<br /> <br /> Mages and werewolves have nothing to do with my comment. I was specifically talking about vampires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T13:34:46-07:00","id":528047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=527346#post527346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's precisely the intelligence of humans, their resourcefulness and their ability to work together that makes them dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the same intelligence that vampires possess and, in the case of elders, surpass (Their limits of intelligence breaking the limits of human intelligence)?<br /> <br /> Are you implying that vampires aren't resourceful, or that they are incapable of working together? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=527346#post527346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Why do you think the Masquerade came about?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you'd like I can quote myself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The <i>reason</i> vampires don't do that is because it would be stupid. Destroying your very best food source is counterproductive to your chances of survival.<br /> <br /> Vampires could enslave all of humanity as well, but then they'd have to destroy too many humans in order to keep the numbers of slaves manageable. Frankly, it's just easier to work more subtly. </div> </div> </div>Or maybe because it makes it easier for elders to enforce control over the rest of the vampire population, or because openly enslaving all of humanity would bring down the wrath of other supernaturals. But most certainly not because humans are any actual threat to vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=527346#post527346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean &quot;theoretically destroy all of humanity,&quot; not &quot;easily destroy all of humanity.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, see, if I meant theoretically I would have said theoretically. I do mean easily. While a single neonate by himself with no assistance would not be able to easily do it, if you account for the unlimited number of other vampires he can spawn and the unlimited number of slaves he can create, that single neonate is much more than just a single neonate - he's an entire, unending army of physically, mentally and socially superior blood-slaves who will follow a single will (that is to say, his).<br /> <br /> This single vampire can spawn a childe, and thus create create a loyal slave of power near equal to his, each of them superior to a normal person. Both of them can create more children, and each of those children can enslave humans with a few drops of their blood, while also making the humans far more powerful (if they so wish).<br /> <br /> The vampire doesn't even have to take a subtle approach - if you discount the other supernaturals living in the world of darkness, a single neonate vs all of humanity in a blatant and open war (after the neonate has had time to gather up a following) would inevitably end in the destruction of humanity. If the world of darkness vampires were so inclined, humanity would no longer exist. But, as I repeat to you, that would be stupid. Humanity is where they get their children from, and where they feed from - to destroy it would be foolish.<br /> <br /> They don't even need disciplines. Just the basic vampire abilities (Blood-buffing, longetivity, massively accelerated healing, resistance to bashing damage, soaking lethal with Stamina) make the average vampire so far superior to the average mortal that it's ridiculous to assume the vampires could lose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=527346#post527346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A single neonate vampire can be neutralized by a pool-cue snapped in two.</div> </div> </div> </div>It annoys me to no end to continually see staking spouted as a vampire weakness.<br /> <br /> <b>If you try to stake a vampire, you will die.</b><br /> <br /> Do you have any idea just how hard it is to stake a vampire? It's a difficulty 9 roll on which you need to get no less than 5 successes, while also dealing a minimum of three levels of damage (vs a creature that can soak said damage with its stamina).<br /> <br /> Even spending willpower, the odds of succeeding that roll are so astonishingly low that it should never, ever be used in combat unless you have already lost the fight and are throwing a hail mary.<br /> <br /> Consider the very highest dice pool a mortal could reach for that roll - think a mortal ghoul with 5 points in Celerity who's blood buffed himself to a six in dexterity and has a 5 in melee. That's 16 dice. If he spends willpower for an automatic success, his average roll will have 2.92 successes (an average of 3), which is two short. Note again that this is with willpower expenditure.<br /> <br /> In the event of a normal mortal doing it (scratch the 5 in celerity and the blood buffing), the max dice pool would be 10. With a willpower expenditure this would result in an average of 2.1 successes, 1.1 without it. Note that these are the maximum values achievable by mortals - the very highest they are capable of reaching and thus the values that will only be possessed by a handful out of the 7.5 billion out there. Even they suck at staking vamps.<br /> <br /> Even all of this is worthless if they don't get the three damage - which, given how much they've focused on melee and dexterity, is unlikely as they'll be lacking the strength for real damage (which they'll need to beat out the lethal damage soaking vampire).<br /> <br /> All this for a far lesser effect than what would happen to basically <i>anything else</i> if it got a wooden stick through the heart (which would be instant, unrelenting death). I frankly don't count &quot;something that would kill literally everything else but will just paralyze you&quot; to be a weakness. That it can be considered one is a testament to the resilience of the Cainites.<br /> <br /> Staking is NOT something to be done in combat. It's how you neutralize vampires who have already lost the fight. Literally every single other method of combat (including the laughably pathetic True Faith, or even just a kid with a slingshot shooting balls of grass) is more likely to net you a legitimate result than trying to stake the vampire (which will most likely end with you failing and promptly being drained dry).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=527346#post527346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He can easily overpower 2 or 3 people, sure, but he can't fight off 20 people at the same time, all by himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a neonate who put all his points into Bardo, Auspex and Obeah. I'm hard pressed to find any other vampire who would lose that fight.<br /> <br /> A Lasombra could wipe a room of twenty mortals like it's nothing, any vampire with Presence 1 (keeping in mind that Presence is an extremely common discipline) would have little to no trouble either, to name two examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=527346#post527346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He can't fight off an entire SWAT team laying into him with modern weaponry, even if he is only taking Bashing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slightly less trivial, but a blood-buffed vampire could still wipe out a SWAT team - and a Lasombra or a vamp with presence easily so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=527346#post527346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And he certainly can't do anything if they stake him while he's sleeping the day away and drag him out into the sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what the unending number of physically enhanced blood-slaves are for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=527346#post527346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal vampire hunters are responsible for driving vampires underground</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they weren't. The spiel the book(s) give is that the inquisition (not vampire hunters specifically, but inquisitors with True Faith) drove vampires underground. Which is slightly less ridiculous if you consider the Dark Ages True Faith rules, which actually makes the power effective when considered in conjunction with daytime penalties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=527346#post527346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">, because the Elders were scared enough that they tossed their neonates at the humans, who promptly lit them up in big old bonfires. That directly led to the formation of the Sabbat, when the younger vampires got rightfully pissed off that their Elders were throwing them under the bus... or onto the pyre, as the case may be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always found that to be a ridiculous part of the vampire lore. Now, yes, it's true, the books do try to make mortals into a legitimate threat against vampires - but they basically just do this by saying the mortals are dangerous and leaving it at that. There's no way any number of mortals could have ever proven to be a threat to even reasonably intelligent neonates, let alone ancient, powerful, all-controlling elders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=527346#post527346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even an Elder's helpless when the sun comes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>An elder has access to enough powerful disciplines that, unless they have an extremely low path rating (2-3), they can still wipe a room full of mortals in the sun (and I do mean in the sun, as in, while the sun is shining down on them and burning them alive).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=527346#post527346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages and werewolves have nothing to do with my comment. I was specifically talking about vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies, I thought you were referring to all supernaturals as having something to fear from humans in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5540-drakilian","user":"Drakilian","date":". 05-25-2015, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5540-drakilian","name":"Drakilian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:01:08-07:00","id":528422,"title":"","content":"<b>The First Tradition</b>: Vampires are very resourceful and capable of working together - the Camarilla is proof of that, and again, it came into being as a direct result of the threat posed by mortals - yes, the Church, but not every Inquisitor had true faith.<br /> <br /> Consider the opening pages of the Guide to the Camarilla:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It (the Camarilla) exists to protect its members from the surging seas of humanity, which by dint of sheer numbers could wipe most of the Kindred off the face of the earth. The Camarilla's single greatest creation, the Masquerade, exists for precisely this purpose. A veil of misdirection and falsehood, the Masquerade hides the very fact of Kindred existence from the mortal world. What humanity can't see, it can't kill, and thus the Kindred are safe. The fact that the necessity of preserving the Masquerade cuts down somewhat on the casualties Camarilla vampires inflict on the mortal population is meerly a byproduct of the need to preserve the illusion. </div> </div> </div>There was no need to keep the neonates under control in the Dark Ages - they were already well controlled, which was why the Elders were able to sacrifice them.<br /> <br /> <b>Neonate vs. The World</b>: This would make a fantastic V:tM story, actually, although it reminds me a bit of the plot from later on in Twilight. A Sabbat neonate out somewhere in the south west slaughtering an entire small town and turning them into a roving army of bloodsuckers. The Camarilla and Sabbat would go into damage control mode faster than you can say &quot;Martial Law.&quot;<br /> Problem is, an army of Neonates won't last long against an airstrike, a napalm bath, or hell, a couple of snipers with phosphorous tracer rounds that deal aggravated damage. It would be terrifying for a short time, until a military-level response was initiated. And we're not even considering the vampire authorities that would come down on them harder than the sun at high-noon.<br /> <br /> The old Vampire 2nd Edition Player's guide had rules for artillery and military grade support weapons. A 120mm tank gun is doing 30 dice of damage. A LAW rocket is doing 15 dice.<br /> <br /> There's a reason they didn't include stats for artillery weapons in the Revised edition Storyteller's Guidebook - if you're going up against Stinger anti-aircraft missiles as a vampire, something has gone seriously off kilter in the chronicle. Even a Methuselah of Mithras's stature was slammed into Torpor by the bombing of London during WW2.<br /> <br /> Lets not even get started on flame throwers.<br /> <br /> <b>Staking</b>: Staking isn't as difficult as you think. Check out V20, pg. 280, or V:tM Revised 213, Staking a vampire requires a single success at difficulty 9 and must score at least 3 health levels of damage. Certainly not easy (especially if the vampire is not restrained and can dodge), but not as impossible as to make it tactically impractical.<br /> <br /> <b>Battle Royale</b>: I think you're sorely overstating the power of a Neonate vampire. You're not going to be able to Dread-gaze a score of people before you're beaten into Torpor. Obtenebration probably has the best crowd-control options with shroud of night - Arms of the Abyss won't cut it I'm afraid. Shroud of Night only covers 10 feet - the vampire's best tactic would be to shroud themselves and then try to pick off the mortals as they ran.<br /> <br /> I'm hard pressed to actually find any other discipline at all that would be as effective as Obliteration against 20 people.<ul><li>Presence is worthless - Awe isn't going to stop them as combat constitutes a dangerous situation.</li> <li>Dread gaze and Enchantment are both single-target powers.</li> <li>Dominate and Dementation are also single target. Obfuscate only helps if you weren't seen to begin with, and then only to escape - it isn't going to let you disappear from view at that level.</li> <li>You're not going to be able to fend all of them off with 3 dots in Celerity.</li> <li>Fortitude 3 might be enough to save you if all your taking is Bashing damage, but...</li> <li>With that many attackers remember that your defensive maneuvers and attacks will be made at Difficulty 10 (+1 per opponent beyond the first to a max of 10). You'll probably be down into Torpor before you inflict much damage in return, no matter what your Disciplines are. Again, I'll give you Obtenebration level 2, but one power from a specialty discipline you'd be hard pressed to find outside the Sabbat doesn't equal an easy victory for your average Neonate against a mob of angry mortals.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Elder in the Sun</b>: An elder fighting in direct sunlight is taking 3 Health levels of damage a turn. He can soak this with Fortitude at difficulty 10. That's not to mention having to check for R\u00f6tschreck. Even with a decent path rating (say 7) that's a serious handicap on dice pools. He's not long for the world in this situation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:13:58-07:00","id":528483,"title":"","content":"So yea, pretty much just seconding most everything RebelWithoutAClan said. I was going to reply bit by bit, but he/she has done a nice job covering the bases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:32:26-07:00","id":528506,"title":"","content":"What does sense of superiority have to do with rationality? Vampire society treats humans as a dangerous but useful resource, they do not treat humans as peers. They are treated as pets at best and things at worse. They believe they are the conspiracy that runs the world. That they have guided human history from the dawn of time. <br /> <br /> Fera treat humanity as at best an obstacle to their holy work(and for the Ratkin a target for their holy work), some might see humans as worthwhile tools but only perhaps the COG see humanity as potential partners in saving Gaia(and even that's debateable).<br /> <br /> Whether or not these are accurate views isn't the question at hand. Real world supremecist groups aren't based on rationality either, so why should groups who's emotions are so extreme they might rip off your head for saying the wrong thing to them have cultures built on rational and patient thought?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T15:14:12-07:00","id":529308,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm more trying to say that among vampires, their sense of superiority took a major blow following the Inquisition. They'd never admit it, of course, but you can tell by their actions that they aren't quite as assured of it deep down as they used to be. By in large they certainly consider themselves superior to humans, but that perception is riddled with cracks and fissures now..<br /> <br /> I'm not so much arguing with you as putting the view of Vampiric superiority into context. I think I misunderstood where you were coming from with the comment about zombies.<br /> <br /> The point I'm making about the zombie analogy is that humans are scary to vampires precisely because their intellect makes them dangerous. Humans are, in the real world, the apex predator because our brains allow us to incorporate and build upon all of nature's aggression. We don't have claws and teeth, so we make them out of stone, bronze, iron, steel, titanium, carbon nanotubes. We learn how to launch those teeth attached to axes and spears, or fire them from bows, crossbows, and guns so that we can bite our prey from safety. We dip our artificial teeth in the poison of tree frogs to make them deadly. We make our artificial teeth burn with fire.<br /> <br /> We don't have thick hide, so we take the hide of our prey. We learn to cure it to make it harder and more durable and protective. We learn to beat bronze, iron and steel into artificial hide, or to make it from ceramics and high durability plastics to make it lighter and more resilient, to the point where it can resist bullets.<br /> <br /> We set traps for our prey. We domesticate animals to help us hunt, like dogs or falcons, because they have senses and capabilities we don't.<br /> <br /> To make a long story short, humans adapt. It's like the book I am Legend (well worth the read - the movie doesn't do it justice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T18:24:29-07:00","id":529476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/522367-do-vampires-kuei-jin-fera-believe-they-are-more-superior-to-humans?p=529308#post529308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm more trying to say that among vampires, their sense of superiority took a major blow following the Inquisition. They'd never admit it, of course, but you can tell by their actions that they aren't quite as assured of it deep down as they used to be. By in large they certainly consider themselves superior to humans, but that perception is riddled with cracks and fissures now..</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem to actually match up with how the Dark Ages rolled out. History more or less worked the way it did in the real world. There weren't open vampire fiefdoms except &quot;somewhere in Eastern Europe&quot;. Its never anyplace important its never in your face. Mithras isn't personally picking kings of England and the hundred years war isn't decided by over the top vampire duels in at night. It has as its always been, the Inquisition was just a culling of them getting little too loud it wasn't a change in direction for them. They were always parasites claiming dominion, the only cities that were ever arguments for anything different are carthage(which doesn't look different than in the real world so maybe the whole vampires walking openly is.. full of shit) and the First and Second ciites(which have as much evidence for existing as Narnia).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}